# Current project state

Consolidation updated September 17, 2026; thesis status below is the last
recorded September 16 state, not a fresh thesis review. The September 17 consolidation covered project status, thesis/review routing,
crate/QP maintenance notes, experiment navigation, and selected agent guidance.
Obsolete instructions and duplicate plans were retired; scientific sources and
raw evidence were preserved. Link/structure checks do not constitute a complete
audit of the remaining research claims. No thesis sprint was launched.

## Outcome

The first whole-thesis PASS deadline (September 14, 18:00 Berlin) was missed.
Jörn later judged the frozen 86-page thesis FAIL. HKO and Chapter 4 have narrower
PASS judgments; Chapter 4 prose was borderline. On September 16 he accepted the
analytic rotated-pentagon proof but rejected its exposition. No whole-thesis PASS
or second-sprint deadline is established.

Jörn now proposes a second-sprint envelope of $3,000 shadow API quota and roughly
six hours elapsed, retaining 120 minutes of his attention. This proposal has not
started a clock; see `docs/sprint-two/KICKOFF.md` for proposed checkpoints.

## Current work and artifact owners

- **Source recovery:** `thesis/candidate/main.tex` is the ordinary-path recovered
  candidate. Its README and `docs/source-recovery/` own build/manifest evidence.
  Recovery preserves frozen content, including known errors; it does not
  integrate new chapters or certify all historical experiment provenance.
- **Pentagon replacement:** `docs/pentagon-chapter-v2/` holds the latest completed
  four-page candidate. Integration instructions live in
  [the candidate map](../thesis/candidate/integration.md). Mathematics was accepted in
  the earlier version; the new prose has no human PASS. No ridge-descriptor
  section belongs here. Main thesis integration is pending.
- **Fresh literature rewrite:** `docs/literature-rewrite/` contains the completed
  Sol synthesis with Luna source extraction: evidence map, LaTeX, bibliography
  and four-page standalone PDF. It has not been integrated or human-approved.
- **Second-run handoff:** `docs/sprint-two/KICKOFF.md` is the coordinator starting
  packet, with subsequent launch/resource checks in
  `docs/sprint-two/readiness.md`. It does not activate a new root, goal or clock
  by existing on disk.

Jörn gives about 120 minutes total attention for sprint two, with usual async
latency of 10 seconds–10 minutes (occasionally an hour) and reading blocks up to
about 30 minutes. The September 16 preparation budget has expired; it is not a
constraint on this consolidation. Jörn rejected being asked to guess delivery
timing; the next coordinator owns a scope-based estimate and its updates. No
second-run deadline should be inferred from either budget.

## Remaining substantive work

